##  ShelfDock rows, top to bottom: the fixed widgets below the accordion.
##
##  Rendered by bin/mk-shelf --static, so this window never swaps aliases and
##  its group headers are section labels rather than controls -- nothing here
##  collapses.  That is exactly why the swallowed widgets live here: a swap
##  strands them (see the note at the top of shelf.items), and a static window
##  holds them steady.
##
##  Sized with --height auto: the window is as tall as the rows below add up
##  to, and mk-shelf publishes that total as $[infostore.shelf_dock_h] so the
##  accordion above can subtract it.  No flex row is allowed here for that
##  reason -- there is no fixed height for it to expand into.
##
##  Format is otherwise identical to shelf.items.

##  Module-wide defaults, as in shelf.items: mk-shelf reissues
##  DestroyModuleConfig on every render, so these cannot live in the config.
* Colorset $[infostore.cs_shelf]
* ActiveColorset $[infostore.cs_shelf_hi]
* Frame 0
* Font $[infostore.shelf_font]
* Padding 4 0



group WorldView World View
##  %pager_h% is the shelf's inner width scaled by the monitor's aspect ratio,
##  computed in ShelfRender: the pager is a 3x3 grid of screen-shaped cells, so
##  its height has to track the screen's shape or the pages come out stretched.
%pager_h%  Swallow(NoClose,UseOld) ShelfPager 'Module FvwmPager ShelfPager', \
     Frame -1, Colorset $[infostore.cs_pager]

group SysMon System Monitor
##  conky, swallowed.  The height matches minimum_height in conkyrc-shelf; the
##  sunken frame here is the trough the three bars sit in, because conky draws
##  a bar's outline and fill in one colour and cannot make its own.
58   Swallow(NoClose,UseOld) ShelfMeters \
     'Exec exec conky -c $[FVWM_USERDIR]/conkyrc-shelf', \
     Frame -1, Colorset $[infostore.cs_shelf_well]

group Media Media
##  Placeholder: playerctl transport + volume.
50   Title "(transport)", Frame -1, Colorset $[infostore.cs_shelf_well]
